Subject: [PATCH] Do not send traversal child semantics nodes to engine when
 traversal parent is missing (#193372)

fix https://github.com/flutter/flutter/issues/190357
When an `OverlayPortal` (such as the one inside a Material `Slider`) is
inside a pushed route, the route's entrance transition (e.g.,
`FadeTransition`) starts at opacity `0.0` on the initial frame.

`RenderAnimatedOpacityMixin.visitChildrenForSemantics` skips visiting
the `OverlayPortal` anchor (`traversalParentIdentifier`), while
`_RenderTheater.visitChildrenForSemantics` still visits the
`OverlayPortal`'s `_RenderDeferredLayoutBox`
(`traversalChildIdentifier`) directly on the `OverlayEntry`.

Although the traversal child is excluded from its hit-test parent's
`childrenInTraversalOrder` and `childrenInHitTestOrder` when its
traversal parent is not in `_traversalParentNodes`,
`SemanticsOwner.sendSemanticsUpdate` still serialized the traversal
child via `_addToUpdate`. This sent an orphan `SemanticsNode` (not
referenced by any parent in the update) to the engine, causing issues.


This PR:
- Skips calling `_addToUpdate` in `SemanticsOwner.sendSemanticsUpdate`
for nodes in a traversal child subtree whose traversal parent is missing
(`_isSkippedInHitTestTree`).
- Marks affected traversal children, their unmerged descendants, and
their hit-test `parent`s dirty when a traversal parent is newly
registered, detaches, or changes its identifier so the nodes and
hit-test child lists are updated in sync when the traversal parent
enters or leaves the semantics tree.


